      "name": "ref-stewardship",
      "title": "Ref stewardship — one ref, many writers, one steward",
      "description": "Steward a WATCHED REF — a long-lived branch many processes write and one consumer serialises. Covers what makes a ref need a steward at all, why a coalescing window is a different object from a hold, the four durable fields a window needs so a handover cannot double-push, and the rule that a steward stores decisions and reads facts live. Use for \"gh-pages is cancelling its own deployments\", \"two sessions pushed the same store branch\", \"who owns writes to this branch\", \"coalesce these pushes\", and before giving any ref a concurrency policy.",
